    932  f442							; --- D6 M1 (left-col block): M1X = 8*(m1_col+1)-1 -> CollisionEndX ($8E) ---
    933  f442							; 0 = no M1 patch. Window: this VBL write -> PositionBallM1 reads it
    934  f442							; later the same VBL (staged-file pattern like Temp/BallX). Overscan
    935  f442							; routines (PHM/LWC/blast/laser) restage their own CollisionEndX values
    936  f442							; AFTER the cave read, so the alias never crosses a frame boundary.
    937  f442							; NOT zeroed with BandTab on strip kill — M1 is a whole-cave latch and
    938  f442							; convert guarantees its cell is solid/unpatched (wall) where it must hide.
    939  f442							; M1 strip DESTROYED (EnemyDeadMask b4, StripBlastCheck's M1 twin) →
    940  f442							; stage 0: PositionBallM1 skips ENAM1, the pack's b3 flag clears, and
    941  f442							; both overlay paths (PHM/blast) treat the strip as gone next frame.
