   1577  fae9							; --- Phase 3: phase-cell blink (moved here — StageBandTab window full)
   1578  fae9							; Walks the hot-stream $80 records [class, 2c, row, 2, 1] and toggles
   1579  fae9							; the cell's two PF bits per EnemyRamP bit5 (64f cycle: 32 ON + 32
   1580  fae9							; OFF). The PF buffers are the collision map — render, PHM, and the
   1581  fae9							; laser all follow the blink for free. $81/$82 (vcrunch/hcrunch)
   1582  fae9							; tramp to bank3 (CrunchClock ping-pong staging — Phase 4); legacy
   1583  fae9							; hot rects are skipped. CollisionEndY ($8F) is
   1584  fae9							; scratch: the pack rebuild in StageBandTab overwrites it right
   1585  fae9							; after the call returns.
   1586  fae9				   PhaseBlink
   1587  fae9							; --- Phase C vcrunch slice staging (defaults; the walk's VcrShutter
   1588  fae9							; arm overwrites for shutter rooms). Runs every VBL this routine does —
   1589  fae9							; bank1 HUD already stomped $EA/$EB/$EC after the cave, so a full
   1590  fae9							; restage here is the only way the next kernel reads sane values.
   1591  fae9							; Idle defaults: VcrBand=$FF (tail dispatch never matches), VcrNext=0
   1592  fae9							; (idle marker — only 1..4 slices), VcrState=0. The band0 length needs
   1593  fae9							; no byte: .Row derives 8/48 from these two.
